OL,3,GNEWSAAttractions still open despite
OL,4,Abluetongue outbreak
OL,5,
OL,6,FIts "business as usual" for zoos and
OL,7,Fanimal attractions across the South
OL,8,FWest despite an ongoing bluetongue
OL,9,Foutbreak among livestock.
OL,11,FAttractions including Paignton and
OL,12,FNewquay Zoos, Totnes Rare Breeds Farm
OL,13,Fand The Big Sheep, near Ilfracombe,
OL,14,Fsaid they had all taken precautions and
OL,15,Fvaccinated their animals most at risk
OL,16,Ffrom the insect-borne viral disease.
OL,18,FThe Department for Environment, Food
OL,19,Fand Rural Affairs (Defra) confirmed
OL,20,Fzoos and attractions could stay open
OL,21,Fbecause there was no risk to visitors.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
